  "authority": "AUDIT_ONLY",
  "ceiling": "AUDIT_ONLY structural/stoichiometric second-signal. It corroborates that the module's canonical structure rule is chemically general (not curve-fit to 3 anchors) and fail-closed, but asserts nothing about product qualification, cure conversion, or wet-lab AHEW of polydisperse commercial grades, which remain measured-only. Live runtime stays LOCKED_INTERNAL; promotion needs the human dual-identity Phase-0 keys.",
  "claim": "An independent RDKit-2026.03.2 reference implementation of the module's stated structure rule (EEW=M/n_epoxide; AHEW=M/n_active_amine_NH, counting 2 per primary + 1 per secondary + 0 per tertiary amine N-H, with amide/imine/nitrile/nitro/aromatic-ring N and hydroxyl H excluded) (1) reproduces every shipped Phase-0 'expected' EEW/AHEW on the 3 exact anchors (max abs error 0.0338 g/eq, bar 0.5) and 6/6 monodisperse records, AND (2) generalises the falsifiable hypothesis beyond those fitted points: a 13-structure published epoxy-hardener grid (aliphatic/cycloaliphatic/araliphatic/aromatic 1'/2'/3' amines incl. DETA, TETA, TEPA, EDA, IPDA, HMDA, m-XDA, piperazine, AEP, DACH, aniline, MDA, DDS) is classified with 100% correct active-N-H integer count and theoretical AHEW within 0.3% of published supplier/handbook reference values; 7/7 non-amine controls (tertiary amine, amide, DMF, urea, nitrile, pyridine, nitro) are fail-closed to 0 active N-H; and the hydroxyl-exclusion probe (ethanolamine) correctly counts 2 amine N-H while ignoring -OH. IUPAC-2021 standard atomic-weight uncertainty propagates to <=0.011 g/eq on all anchors, i.e. the 0.5 g/eq acceptance bar carries >=47x headroom over the fundamental atomic-mass uncertainty; the exact-arithmetic claim is limited only by rounding of the published reference values, not by atomic-mass knowledge.",
